Subagents run inside the Claude Code CLI process: a Bash call from one sees
the same CLAUDE_PID as the lead agent. A pid-based claim cannot tell a
subagent from its parent — two claims, same pid, both live. Subagents claim
with PIDLY_AGENT plus a lease, the path already built for cloud agents,
which turns out to cover shared process tables as well as absent ones.

Not a hook. SubagentStart and SubagentStop exist, but PreToolUse cannot
modify tool input, so a hook cannot put the number into a subagent's prompt.
It does not need to: the lead agent writes that prompt. And a ticket per
subagent is the wrong default — most subagent calls are lookups, numbers are
never reused, tickets are never deleted, and an open child blocks its parent
from closing, so automatic tracking would make permanent noise that also
wedges the work.

PIDLY_PID now defaults to CLAUDE_PID where set, falling back to $PPID. The
two usually resolve to the same process, but only because a tool call's
shell is a direct child of the runner.

That change broke a test that had been relying on the coincidence: it used a
per-command assignment, so the claim carried it and the release did not.
Exporting once for the agent's lifetime is what the reference already says
to do.

Done: guidance in the reference and the summary, covered by the existing
suites.
